1
00:00:05,634 --> 00:00:07,980
每次拿报纸都给库斯曼 做免费心理治疗.
I gotta figure out a way to get the morning paper...

2
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:10,360
下次得想想办法
without having to give Ellen Koosman a free diagnosis.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:13,240
我的报道刊登了吗？
Well, is my story in?

4
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:17,760
-好像搞错了 -什么？
- Oh, they've made a terrible mistake. - What? What?

5
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:20,800
他们把你的报道放在头条了!
Well, they put your story on the front page!

6
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:24,040
说真的？
Are you serious?

7
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:33,420
<纽约建筑巨头贿赂政府官员>
"Major Long Island developer offers bribe to County officials...

8
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:35,860
作者：麦姬.海狸
"by Margaret Beaver."

9
00:00:37,220 --> 00:00:38,180
不!
Oh, no!

10
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:41,150
是麦姬.西弗
No, it's Margaret Seaver.

11
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:43,820
这还多亏了你
Oh, honey, I owe you for this.

12
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:46,820
要不是你留在家，让我出去工作.
If you hadn't moved your practice home so I could try my career again...

13
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:48,600
我哪来的上头版？
I'd never be on Page 1.

14
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:50,580
若是真的心存感激.
Well, if you really think you owe me one...

15
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:54,860
你大可以署名“杰森.西弗的老婆”
next time they give you a by-line why don't you have it read, Mrs. Jason Seaver?

16
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:57,060
快点把话说完
Don't hold your breath.

17
00:00:58,060 --> 00:00:59,320
感激已经没有了
So much for gratitude.

18
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:01,840
我要换装上班
Well, I'd better change before work.

19
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:03,860
这不是工作服？
These aren't your work clothes?

20
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:08,280
今早更衣时，我还是第六版的作者
Well, when I put this on this morning, I was a Page 6 writer...

21
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:10,160
现在要换成头版的装扮
and now I have to dress for Page 1.

22
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:15,040
我需要一份工作
I need a good job.

23
00:01:15,337 --> 00:01:19,744
-孩子啊，还是读书好啊 -不，不
- No, don't be a fool. Stay in school. - No, no.

24
00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:22,200
今天我们要调查人们工作的一天.
Today's the day we're supposed to observe someone at work...

25
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:24,412
准备明天劳动节发言
so we can do a talk about it tomorrow at Career Day.

26
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:25,120
那？
So?

27
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:27,080
我原本打算调查凯西的爸爸
I was all set to do mine on Cathy Dunne's dad.

28
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:29,620
他是个股票经纪人
He's a stockbroker.

29
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:33,100
可是凯西刚刚来电 她爸虽然工龄32年.
And Cathy just called to tell me that they fired her father...

30
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:35,020
却一下子被解雇了
after 32 years with the company.

31
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:37,620
我今早真是倒霉
Talk about wrecking my morning.

32
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:42,940
其他人的工作也满有意思的
Well, you know, you do know some other people with interesting jobs.

33
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:44,520
说一个看看
Name one.

34
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:48,280
你身边有个人，他专注于他的职业
Somebody very close to you happens to be a dedicated professional...

35
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:52,180
他讲究穿着，他是一家之主
who also heads up a family and is a pretty snappy dresser.

36
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:55,620
对了!妈妈!
Of course! Mom!

37
00:01:58,120 --> 00:01:59,800
我是说我
I was talking about me, Carol.

38
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:02,480
爸爸，我需要真正的那种工作
But, Dad, I need someone with a real job.

39
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:04,500
妈？
Mother?

40
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:07,846
坏八怪!
Phlegm-face!

41
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:12,080
爸爸，我不舒服
Dad, I think I'm sick.

42
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:17,040
凯罗 有些人认为心理医生是真正的职业
Carol, you know, some people think psychiatry is a real job.

43
00:02:17,860 --> 00:02:20,320
不信就算了
Fine, fine, don't believe me.

44
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:24,220
爸，我病了，量量我的体温
Dad, I'm sick. Here, take my temperature.

45
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:28,140
好的，测体温还是肛温？
Okay. Oral or the old-fashioned way?

46
00:02:30,148 --> 00:02:33,033
(English Subtitle) Growing.Pains.S01E2 -= The.Career.Decision =- Subripped by zerox

47
00:03:11,553 --> 00:03:14,321
太棒了，不用上学!
All right, no school!

48
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:21,300
我要一份煎蛋，要全熟的 两片猪肉.
I'll have a fried egg, over easy, two strips of bacon...

49
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:24,420
一片肉桂面包再加一点果冻
a slice of cinnamon toast with just a touch of jelly.

50
00:03:24,740 --> 00:03:27,420
-炉子里有麦粥 -太好了
- There's oatmeal on the stove. - Perfect.

51
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:32,380
妈妈也说是好主意
Mom says it's a great idea.

52
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:35,540
麦克，我今天不用上学
Mike, I'm not going to school today.

53
00:03:35,660 --> 00:03:38,000
我一整天只需要帮妈妈录音
I'm spending the whole day recording Mom.

54
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:41,620
我一整天只需要无所事事
I'm spending the whole day at home doing nothing.

55
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:43,700
大家好
Hi, guys.

56
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:47,820
亲爱的，我得上路了 免得流言蜚语.
Oh, honey, I gotta run. I don't want people saying:

57
00:03:47,820 --> 00:03:51,140
“麦姬这下红了 上班就可以姗姗来迟”
"Now that Maggie's a star reporter, she's coming in late."

58
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:55,240
于是迅速吻了她的家人.
Thus with a quick kiss to the people she calls her family...

59
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:59,440
记者忙碌的一天要揭开帷幕了
a hectic day in the typical pell-mell world of a great reporter begins.

60
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:03,760
杰森，请帮忙洗衣服
Oh, and Jason, could you do that extra load of laundry, if you get a chance?

61
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:07,520
家庭琐事抛诸脑后，她出发了
With petty thoughts of home behind her, she heads off...

62
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:10,840
迈入了这个残酷的.
into the cruel unknown that is...

63
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:12,300
未知的世界
the real world.

64
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,580
-你在干什么？ -康复中
- What are you doing? - Healing.

65
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:21,220
若是有精力打游戏机.
Mike, if you're well enough for video games...

66
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:23,320
我15分钟内送你到学校吧
I can have you at school in 15 minutes.

67
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:26,460
爸爸，我给你添麻烦了
Oh, I hope I'm not too much trouble, Dad.

68
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:31,140
若是头脑清醒了，课本就放在你跟前
If your head clears, remember those school books are right in front of you.

69
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:33,340
我感到耳边嗡嗡作响
Now I'm hearing bells.

70
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:39,980
库斯曼，我现在很忙..进来吧
Ellen Koosman. I'm so busy right now, I've been... Please, come in.

71
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,340
马上就好了
I can only stay a second.

72
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:45,020
我是过来借酵母粉的
I wanted to know if I could borrow some dry yeast from you.

73
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:48,420
本来今早打算去市场，只是脚太累了
I was gonna go to the store this morning, but my legs were so tired.

74
00:04:48,460 --> 00:04:50,880
也许是吃了医生的药所致.
I don't know if it's the pills that the doctor gave me...

75
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:52,640
也许是天气不好所致
or if it's the weather that's causing...

76
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:54,200
-嗨，麦克 -嗨，我病了
- Hi, Mike. - Hey, I'm sick.

77
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:56,820
-我去拿酵母粉 -谢谢
- I'll get some yeast. - Thank you.

78
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:59,540
我要烘些面包送汤
I wanted to bake some bread to go with the soup that I'm making.

79
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:04,740
我感冒了，真是难以置信.
Now I'm coming down with a cold. Can you believe it?

80
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:07,700
这个冬天真是祸不单行
All winter long it's been one thing after the other.

81
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:12,340
大脚趾头也发炎了
And now I've got a bunion on my big toe.

82
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:18,500
西弗医生，你得救救我
Dr. Seaver, you've got to help me.

83
00:05:19,060 --> 00:05:22,100
我原来是个男儿身的姑娘
I feel like a woman trapped in a man's body.

84
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:26,300
也是个坏陋的姑娘
Not a very pretty one, either.

85
00:05:27,655 --> 00:05:29,324
-哈尔，你好 -杰森，你好
- How you doing, Hal? - How are you, Jason?

86
00:05:29,324 --> 00:05:31,540
见到你太好了，进来吧
Good to see you. Come on in.

87
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:32,860
还记得麦姬吗？
You remember Maggie.

88
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:35,180
我还以为自己记得呢
I thought I did.

89
00:05:36,460 --> 00:05:39,460
其实这是隔壁的库斯曼 这是哈尔医生
Actually, this is Ellen Koosman, our next door neighbor. Dr. Miller.

90
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:41,320
你也是个医生？
Oh, so you're a doctor, too.

91
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:44,300
我这下面疼得厉害.
I have this terrible pain right here below...

92
00:05:44,305 --> 00:05:46,780
哈尔医生是兽医
Dr. Miller is a veterinarian.

93
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:48,700
我家的德国狗掉毛了
There's a bald spot on my schnauzer.

94
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:51,100
满逗人的，就在这个位置.
It's really funny. Right here. It's got this thing that's...

95
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:52,440
你赶时间是吧？
I know you can't stay.

96
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:55,260
-幸会 -幸会
- Nice to meet you, Doctor. - Nice meeting you.

97
00:05:56,620 --> 00:05:59,060
幸好你没告诉她我是心理医生
Thanks for not telling her I'm a psychiatrist.

98
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:00,380
我现在没有病人
I'm in between patients now.

99
00:06:00,380 --> 00:06:01,420
-进办公室聊吗？ -好的
- You want to come in the office? - Yeah, sure.

100
00:06:12,620 --> 00:06:17,140
-这就是你的办公室？ -哈尔，在家工作很舒服
- This is your office? - Hal, working at home is great, really.

101
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:20,640
我明白你为什么厉害纽约的公司了
I can see why you left your position at Long Island General.

102
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:22,080
来吧，废话少说
All right, let's get it over with.

103
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:23,020
你这次要来说服我.
You're gonna tell me all the reasons...

104
00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:24,440
离职是愚蠢的.
you think I was foolish to quit.

105
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:26,500
不，我是来让你看看我的新作
No, I'd rather show you my latest book.

106
00:06:27,764 --> 00:06:29,025
Wow.

107
00:06:29,280 --> 00:06:31,260
<中年性无能>
"Sexual Dysfunctions of Middle Age."

108
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:33,860
也许对你有帮助
I figured you could use it.

109
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:37,620
幸好你对这个了解深入
Well, at least you're now writing something that you know about.

110
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:45,140
-让护士开门就行了 -她午休去了
- Why don't you let your nurse get that? - She's at lunch.

111
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:48,720
-现在是早上9点 -她是胖了点，但我喜欢
- It's 9:00 a.m. - She's a large woman, but I love her.

112
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:57,540
早上好!我是屋顶维修公司的杰里
Good morning, sir. How are you? I'm Jerry from Rapid Roofing.

113
00:06:57,980 --> 00:07:01,120
-我家屋顶很好，谢谢 -车房天花漏水
- Well, our roof is fine, thank you. - Your garage leaks like a sieve.

114
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:02,640
谁说的？
Who said that?

115
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,060
隔壁光头狗的主人
The lady next door with the baldheaded dog.

116
00:07:06,087 --> 00:07:08,456
-她不清楚.. -我马上就给你检查
- Well, she wouldn't know... - I'll check it out right now.

117
00:07:08,456 --> 00:07:10,721
听我说.
No, it's... Listen. Hey.

118
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:13,720
爸，我现在有精神看电视了
Hey, Dad, I think I'm well enough to watch TV now.

119
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:15,660
不能看好看的节目
As long as you don't enjoy it.

120
00:07:18,680 --> 00:07:21,760
大夫，在这里行医真是刺激
Oh, it's a real exciting little practice you got here, Doctor.

121
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:23,600
平时没那么冷清的
Well, it's not usually this quiet.

122
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:27,100
平时这房间里到处是疯子
Most of the time this house is crawling with people with mental problems.

123
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:28,660
想得美
Yeah, you wish.

124
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:32,860
好吧，客套话到此为之
All right, Jason, enough of this male bonding.

125
00:07:34,580 --> 00:07:38,280
我要离开纽约的心理治疗院
I wanted to tell you that I'm leaving Long Island General.

126
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:41,960
-这么多年了.. -对，是时候.
- After all those years? - Yeah, I think it's time to move on.

127
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:44,360
做一些有意义的事情了
Do something really worthwhile for a change.

128
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:46,420
我要去洛杉矶做电台节目
I'm gonna do talk radio in LA.

129
00:07:48,730 --> 00:07:49,860
洛杉矶
LA.

130
00:07:49,860 --> 00:07:52,120
那里疯子多的是
You never run out of patients out there.

131
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:58,040
人事部要我推荐继任者.
Now, look, the board of directors wants me to pick my successor...

132
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:00,360
我推荐你
and I'm picking you.

133
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:03,060
-我？ -对，舍你其谁？
- Me? - Yeah, who better?

134
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:06,100
你曾对我说.
You know, you once told me you wanted to run this department...

135
00:08:06,100 --> 00:08:07,280
40岁前要成为老总
by the time you were 40.

136
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:09,620
看来你可以提前3年了
Well, you're gonna be three years ahead of schedule.

137
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:15,140
-真的？ -我从来不拿工作或内衣来开玩笑
- Are you kidding? - I never kid about work or underwear.

138
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:18,400
这个.
This is...

139
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:21,740
这个太棒了，这机会.
This is incredible. This is the kind of opportunity I've...

140
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:25,340
-我不能接受 -什么？
- I can't take the job. - What?

141
00:08:26,033 --> 00:08:30,860
我和麦姬现在有了协议
Now, you see... You see, Maggie... I have a deal with her now, Hal.

142
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:32,800
轮到她发展事业
She's taking a shot at her career.

143
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:36,020
杰森，这可是整个部门的总管
Jason, this is head of the entire department.

144
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:37,660
我办不到
I can't.

145
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:42,440
她现在正在腾飞，今早还上头版了
She's really rolling now, Hal. She was on the front page this morning.

146
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:43,420
-有看到吗？ -没看到
- Did you see it? - No, no.

147
00:08:43,985 --> 00:08:47,757
杰森，机会难得啊
Look, Jason, how often do you get a chance like this?

148
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:50,180
37岁当部门主管
Department head at 37.

149
00:08:51,759 --> 00:08:54,060
简直..匪夷所思
It's... It's impossible, Hal.

150
00:08:54,060 --> 00:08:58,020
杰森，至少考虑一下吧
Jason, promise me you'll at least think about it.

151
00:09:00,301 --> 00:09:03,571
我现在的人生.
Hal, my life right now is...

152
00:09:03,571 --> 00:09:07,131
腐烂了!整个排水的东西没了
Dry rot! You're about to lose the whole weenie!

153
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:12,180
回到旋风的中心.
We're back in the eye of the storm...

154
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:16,140
烦嚣的小区日报编辑部
the frantic, fast-paced newsroom of the Long Island Daily Herald.

155
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:19,800
数十名记者呼啸而过
Dozens of reporters race around the room, feverishly.

156
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:24,040
-妈，你正在干什么？ -在找茶包
- Now what are you doing, Mom? - Looking for a tea bag.

157
00:09:26,780 --> 00:09:27,620
找到了
Here it is.

158
00:09:28,380 --> 00:09:29,560
下面要做些什么？
Then what are you gonna do?

159
00:09:30,531 --> 00:09:33,680
首先泡一杯茶.
Well, first I'm going to make myself a cup of tea...

160
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:35,860
接着要找总编苏珊.
and then I'm gonna talk to Susan Rush...

161
00:09:35,980 --> 00:09:38,800
谈谈我的报道的续集
my city editor, about the follow-up story I'm working on.

162
00:09:39,580 --> 00:09:41,700
对了，你应该找苏珊聊聊
Hey, Carol, you should talk to Susan.

163
00:09:41,980 --> 00:09:44,740
她能让你了解报业生涯
She could tell you all about a newspaper career.

164
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:49,140
她身为编辑，女性，年轻，咬字清晰.
She's an editor, a woman, young, articulate...

165
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:51,760
平时人很好
and she's a very sweet person.

166
00:09:58,780 --> 00:09:59,380
麦姬
Maggie.

167
00:09:59,380 --> 00:10:01,020
关于你的文章
About your article.

168
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:04,980
有位约瑟夫.查德威打电话来了.
I just got a call from a Joseph K. Chadway...

169
00:10:05,420 --> 00:10:08,140
就是我负责的头版今早文章中的.
the builder you accused of bribing County officials...

170
00:10:08,140 --> 00:10:11,100
你指责那个贿赂官员的建筑商
in the story I ran on Page 1 this morning.

171
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:16,500
约瑟夫.查德威对指控表示震惊.
Joseph K. Chadway was a little angry at being accused of bribery...

172
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:17,520
这当然了
I'll bet.

173
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:21,260
因为你把他的名字拼错了
...since the man you meant to accuse was Joseph A. Chadway.

174
00:10:22,083 --> 00:10:23,892
我的妈呀
Holy moley.

175
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:26,680
我们的律师也是这种反应
Exactly what our lawyer said.

176
00:10:26,860 --> 00:10:29,200
苏珊，我也不知道为什么.
Oh, Susan, I don't know how this possibly could have...

177
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:32,120
你竟然没有校对名字.
I just can't believe you didn't double-check the name.

178
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:34,360
这是基本常识呀
I mean, that's about as basic as it gets.

179
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:40,400
麦姬，续集不会交给你了.
Maggie, I am pulling you from the follow-up...

180
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:43,000
我得找一个真正的记者
and getting a real reporter.

181
00:10:47,375 --> 00:10:51,246
她人确实很好，对不对？
Well, was I right? Is she nice or what?

182
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:32,800
播放中
It's on.

183
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:43,800
还在播
It's still on. Whoa!

184
00:11:47,620 --> 00:11:50,380
她又要辞职了.
She'd have to quit again.

185
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:55,860
现在轮到我 另一个接受这份工的理由
And... Now I'm talking to myself. That's another reason to take the job.

186
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:59,680
-爸爸 -什么事？
- Hey, Dad. - What is it, Mike?

187
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:02,740
每天下午3：30 电视都会播放<梦幻岛>
Gilligan's Island is on every day at 3:30.

188
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:06,680
麦克，我很忙 我正面临一个痛苦的抉择
Mike, I'm very busy. I'm trying to make a tough decision here.

189
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:08,220
不管我看不看电视，它都在播放
Dad, Dad, it's on whether I watch it or not.

190
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:12,860
节目中的主角，那个富翁 他老婆，教授还有.
Gilligan, the Skipper, too. The millionaire, his wife, the Professor and...

191
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:14,220
-玛丽？ -对
- Mary Ann? - Exactly.

192
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:18,660
-你想说说什么？ -电视剧不是为了我而存在的
- What's the point? - Dad, it's not on for me.

193
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:20,900
总之就是播放中
It's just on.

194
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:27,160
麦克，开始意识到 世界不是以你为中心？
Mike, are you starting to realize that the world doesn't revolve around you?

195
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:30,020
是的
Yeah, I guess I am.

196
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:32,700
恭喜你
Well, congratulations.

197
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:36,140
你刚刚领悟到了加缪的哲学基本原理
You know, you've hit on one of the basic ideas in the philosophy of Camus.

198
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:37,940
加缪是那条杀人鲸？
The killer whale?

199
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:42,160
不，那是沙缪
No, Mike, that's Shamu.

200
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:47,980
失陪了，我要去弄干衣机
Excuse me, I have to empty the dryer.

201
00:12:51,300 --> 00:12:54,780
-来，我可以展示给你看 -不了，谢谢
- Here, Dad, look, I can even show you. - That's okay, thanks.

202
00:12:56,837 --> 00:12:58,791
校车!
The school bus.

203
00:12:59,220 --> 00:13:02,000
-爸爸! -怎么了？
- Hey, Dad! - What? What is it?

204
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:03,360
你还不明白？
Don't you see?

205
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:06,700
若电视是这样，学校也一样
If Gilligan goes on without me, so does my school.

206
00:13:06,700 --> 00:13:10,460
今天即使我不在 人们还是一样地过活
You know, all day today, life went on even though I wasn't there.

207
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:15,500
这是你第一次领悟哲学 我为你而自豪
Mike, this is your first philosophical realization. I'm proud of you.

208
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:17,860
看电视真的能学到东西
See, you can learn from TV.

209
00:13:19,026 --> 00:13:22,578
今天世界没有了我还在转动
Dad, all day today life went on without me.

210
00:13:22,660 --> 00:13:23,580
你也是.
And you, too.

211
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:25,700
-这个我不确定.. -爸爸
- Well, I'm not sure... - But, Dad.

212
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:28,135
你懂吗？这世界不需要我们
Don't you understand? The world doesn't need us anymore.

213
00:13:28,135 --> 00:13:31,786
-没有我们也是好好的 -不要张冠李戴
- It does just fine without us. - Oh, speak for yourself, Mike.

214
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:36,400
这么一天就这么难受，你呢？
Gosh, if I feel like this after one day, how do you feel?

215
00:13:36,780 --> 00:13:38,440
你是天天困在这里
I mean, you're stuck here every day.

216
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:43,580
困在这里？非也，我是选择在这里
Stuck! Michael, I'm not stuck. I'm here because I wanna be here.

217
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:47,540
不好意思，洗衣机叫我了
Now if you'll excuse me, my laundry's calling.

218
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:49,520
袜子兄弟，来了
Coming, socks.

219
00:13:52,860 --> 00:13:56,500
就像漂流到“梦幻岛”上面的人
Trapped just like the castaways on Gilligan's isle.

220
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:58,340
为期3小时
A three-hour tour.

221
00:14:00,900 --> 00:14:03,640
-爸爸! -凯罗，提早回家了？
- Dad, Dad! - Hi, Carol. You're home early.

222
00:14:03,640 --> 00:14:05,300
-妈妈呢？ -在停车
- Where's Mom? - Parking her car.

223
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:07,480
听好，没时间解释了.
Listen, I don't have much time to explain...

224
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:11,112
今天是妈妈一辈子中最糟糕的一天
but Mom has had the worst day of her entire life.

225
00:14:11,112 --> 00:14:12,060
为什么？
Why?

226
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:14,548
不要在刺激她了，可以吗？
Now, you can't do or say anything to upset her, okay?

227
00:14:14,548 --> 00:14:16,547
什么事了？
But what happened?

228
00:14:17,220 --> 00:14:20,400
-亲爱的 -提前下班了？
- Hi, honey. - Hi, home early, huh?

229
00:14:20,621 --> 00:14:23,824
爸爸，不是说不要刺激她吗!
Dad, I told you not to upset her!

230
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:26,580
凯罗，我没事
Carol, I'm okay.

231
00:14:26,700 --> 00:14:30,740
谢谢你的关心 不过我一直都说了，我没事
Now I appreciate your concern, but as I told you all afternoon, I'm fine.

232
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:32,160
什么事了？
What happened?

233
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:35,660
我和编辑有点矛盾
Oh, I had a disagreement with my editor.

234
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:38,980
她把妈妈骂得狗血临头.
Dad, she made Mom look like a complete...

235
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:39,420
凯罗
Carol.

236
00:14:40,100 --> 00:14:42,120
录了音，你听听看
I've got it on tape, Dad. You decide.

237
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:46,747
凯罗，成年人说话你是不会懂的
No. Now, Carol, you just don't understand how adults talk to adults.

238
00:14:46,747 --> 00:14:48,839
有时候成年人会骂人
Sometimes they yell.

239
00:14:48,900 --> 00:14:50,780
没看过李敖的节目吗？
Haven't you seen the new Jack Klugman show?

240
00:14:53,060 --> 00:14:55,580
原来是这样
Sure, sure, that must be it.

241
00:14:57,560 --> 00:14:59,980
-什么事了？ -没什么
- What happened? - Oh, no big deal.

242
00:14:59,980 --> 00:15:02,200
那好，听她的口气.
That's good. You know, the way she's carrying on...

243
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:03,780
-还以为是世界末日了 -不是
- I thought it was the end of the world. - No.

244
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:08,560
还记得心理治疗院里的哈尔吗？
Hey, you remember Hal Miller, doctor from Long Island General?

245
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:10,260
他今天过来了，还说.
Well, he came by here today, and he offered me...

246
00:15:10,260 --> 00:15:12,000
-杰森.. -怎么了？
- Oh, Jason. - What?

247
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:14,820
今天是我最耻辱的一天
I have never been so humiliated in all my life.

248
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:15,660
亲爱的，怎么了？
Honey, what?

249
00:15:15,660 --> 00:15:17,840
这不是说因为被骂.
It is not being yelled at that really bothered me, but...

250
00:15:17,912 --> 00:15:19,660
甚至不是因为我的过错
Or even making the mistake to begin with.

251
00:15:19,660 --> 00:15:22,420
-什么过错？ -我把K写成A了
- What mistake? - I used a "K" instead of an "A."

252
00:15:24,020 --> 00:15:24,440
不是吧!
No!

253
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:27,320
-拼错了男人的名字 -那还好
- In a man's name. - Well, that's not so bad.

254
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:29,660
但文章是指控他的，他也许会告我们
Who will probably sue us because we said he was a felon.

255
00:15:29,660 --> 00:15:31,400
那就麻烦了
That could be trouble.

256
00:15:32,020 --> 00:15:35,120
-知道我最害怕什么吗？ -不知道
- But you know what really got to me? - No.

257
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:37,780
苏珊骂我的时候，我一直在想.
It's what kept going through my head when Susan was yelling at me.

258
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:38,280
想什么？
What?

259
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:41,700
我不应该工作，应该在家洗衣服
That instead of working I could be home doing the laundry.

260
00:15:42,800 --> 00:15:44,660
而且听起来很合理
And it sounded good.

261
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:47,600
你看得不够透彻
Oh, you weren't thinking straight.

262
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:51,820
杰森，我碰到问题，需要你的意见
Oh, Jason, it's time I faced a few things and I need your advice.

263
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:53,480
-好 -好？
- Okay. - Okay?

264
00:15:54,540 --> 00:15:57,960
在过去的一年中，我很害怕回去工作
Over this past year I've had a lot of fears about going back to work.

265
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:01,580
我能够继续18年前的职业吗？
Can I pick up right where I left off 18 years ago?

266
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:06,160
我能够兴比我小…四分之一的人竞争吗？
Can I compete with people half... Three-quarters my age?

267
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:11,040
我是喜欢我的工作 还是为了工作而工作？
Do I really want a career or is it the idea of having a career that I love?

268
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:14,720
这对孩子们公平吗？ 这对你公平吗？
Am I being fair to the kids? Am I being fair to you?

269
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:17,500
于是我模仿你
So I did what you always do.

270
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:20,820
-我列了两张表 -很好
- I started two lists. - Good.

271
00:16:22,140 --> 00:16:25,200
一是继续工作的理由
One of reasons to keep my job.

272
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:28,320
空白的
See, it's blank.

273
00:16:29,516 --> 00:16:32,248
另一张是辞职的理由
And the other of reasons to quit.

274
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:35,240
瞧瞧
Look at it.

275
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:38,840
-面包，牛奶，丝袜.. -不，反面
- "Bread, milk, pantyhose." - No, no, no, the other side.

276
00:16:44,632 --> 00:16:47,825
还真多呢
Well, this is quite a list.

277
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,740
你认为呢？
So, what do you think?

278
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:55,820
让我决定你应否辞职？
Are you asking me if I think you should quit?

279
00:16:57,240 --> 00:16:57,680
对
Yeah.

280
00:16:58,480 --> 00:17:03,020
为什么偏偏在今天问我
Well, it's interesting that you should ask me this today of all days.

281
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:07,000
亲爱的，我需要你的意见 你能给我公正，客观的意见
Oh, honey, I need your advice. I know you'll be fair and objective.

282
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:07,960
是的
Yes.

283
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:11,060
在你不希望我回去时.
See, you were the one that advised me to go back to work...

284
00:17:11,060 --> 00:17:12,920
是你建议我回去工作的
when in your heart of hearts you didn't want me to.

285
00:17:13,120 --> 00:17:16,380
-是的 -这点我很欣赏
- Well, I did, yes. - Yes, and I love you for it.

286
00:17:16,940 --> 00:17:17,600
谢谢
Thank you.

287
00:17:17,600 --> 00:17:20,200
我相信这一次你也能公正，客观
So I know you'll be fair and objective here, too...

288
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:22,600
尽管你真的很想我辞职
even if you really wanted me to quit...

289
00:17:22,640 --> 00:17:25,100
因为你在家真的不好受
because I know staying at home has to be getting to you.

290
00:17:25,806 --> 00:17:28,350
-我.. -我因该辞职吗？
- Well, I've... - Should I quit?

291
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:32,400
-这真的难以定夺 -亲爱的，你认为怎样？
- That's tough, Maggie. - Honey, what do you think?

292
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:38,880
我认为如果你认为.
Well, I think that if you think...

293
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:41,755
回去工作是错误的.
that you've made a mistake going back to work...

294
00:17:41,755 --> 00:17:45,522
那么你应该.
then I think... Then you should...

295
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:49,420
做些相应的补救
do something about it.

296
00:17:54,020 --> 00:17:54,580
那.
Well.

297
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:56,720
不必说下去了
I guess that's all there is to say.

298
00:17:57,600 --> 00:18:02,020
妈妈，我刚听到消息 虽然你是个破记者，我还是爱你
Mom, I just heard, and I still love you even if you are a rotten reporter.

299
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:07,420
-早上好 -省省吧，只有我在
- Good morning. - Save it. It's just me.

300
00:18:08,060 --> 00:18:11,340
-位置是我的 -我帮你坐暖和而已
- Then get out of my chair. - I was just warming it for you.

301
00:18:12,860 --> 00:18:13,980
位置是我的，走开
Out of my chair, squirt.

302
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:17,220
妈妈呢？
Where's Mom?

303
00:18:17,460 --> 00:18:20,340
她提早去上班，要跟上司说清楚
She left for work early to clear some things up with her boss.

304
00:18:21,180 --> 00:18:23,480
-你怎么知道？ -我个子小
- How do you know? - I'm small.

305
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:26,580
人们常常忽略我 什么事情都说出来了
People forget I'm around and say all kinds of things.

306
00:18:28,180 --> 00:18:30,880
大家应该对妈妈说我们信任她
You guys should have told her that you still believe in her...

307
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:32,120
我们支持她
and that you're behind her.

308
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:35,280
有爸爸在，我们就不必了
Hey, Mom doesn't need to hear that from us as long as Dad's around.

309
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:37,740
这才是人们结婚的原因
That's what he's here for. That's why people get married.

310
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:40,600
结婚后，即使知道自己一文不值.
So that there's at least one person saying you're okay...

311
00:18:40,600 --> 00:18:42,320
至少还会有一个人支持自己
when you know you're just a crummy bag of dog meat.

312
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,480
麦克，你说得对
Mike, you're absolutely right.

313
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:49,980
吃完收拾桌子，出去要锁门
You guys are gonna have to clean up here and lock the door when you leave.

314
00:18:50,020 --> 00:18:52,480
我要追上妈妈，不然就迟了
I'm gonna go catch Mom before she makes a mistake.

315
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:57,464
小小的挫折，不该就此放弃
She shouldn't give up because of one little mistake.

316
00:18:57,464 --> 00:18:58,920
这个妈妈知道
Hey, she knows that.

317
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:00,800
生了你以后，她不是继续生孩子吗？
I mean, after you were born she had another kid, didn't she?

318
00:19:03,340 --> 00:19:04,220
可笑
That's funny.

319
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:10,880
拿着
Here.

320
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:15,240
昨天你说要请真正的记者来报道续篇
You said yesterday that you wanted a real reporter to do the follow-up to my story.

321
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:17,200
我就是真正的记者
Well, you've got one, me.

322
00:19:17,640 --> 00:19:19,860
若是这里面还有错误 我就永远离开这里
You find anything wrong with that and I'm out of here for good.

323
00:19:20,140 --> 00:19:23,040
若是里面没有错误，希望你能纳用
But if you don't find anything wrong with it, I expect you to use it...

324
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:25,220
写得不比这里的任何人差
because it's as good as anybody can do in this office.

325
00:19:25,520 --> 00:19:25,960
说得对
You're right.

326
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:29,240
你这样做是不公正的..什么？
And I don't think it's very fair that you just... What?

327
00:19:31,940 --> 00:19:33,180
我说“说得对”
I said, "You're right."

328
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:34,940
Oh.

329
00:19:36,260 --> 00:19:38,600
她是胡说的，别当真
She doesn't know what she's saying. She doesn't mean a word of it.

330
00:19:39,280 --> 00:19:40,900
-什么？ -我是说真的
- What? - Yes, I do.

331
00:19:40,980 --> 00:19:42,960
-不是的 -是的
- No, you don't. - Yes, I do.

332
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:46,280
我只是不想让你辞职
I just want you to know that I don't want you to quit.

333
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:48,780
辞职？我没有要辞职
Quit! I am not going to quit.

334
00:19:49,120 --> 00:19:50,220
-没有？ -没有
- No? - No.

335
00:19:50,500 --> 00:19:50,980
不
No.

336
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:54,900
这里不是“每日行星报”？
This isn't the Daily Planet?

337
00:19:58,700 --> 00:19:59,660
不好意思
Excuse me.

338
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:02,000
路易斯？
Lois?

339
00:20:03,900 --> 00:20:04,460
克拉克？
Clark?

340
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:06,140
吉米？
Jimmy?

341
00:20:06,433 --> 00:20:08,758
不好意思
Excuse me.

342
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:11,980
杰森，你在想些什么？
Jason, what were you thinking?

343
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:16,480
-那一点不好了？ -你想让我被解雇？
- At which embarrassing point? - Are you trying to get me fired?

344
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:18,280
不，我要阻止你辞职
No, I came down here to keep you from quitting.

345
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:20,260
昨天你才建议我辞职
Yesterday you told me to quit.

346
00:20:20,300 --> 00:20:22,740
-那是个坏主意 -我都听你的
- Well, that was bad advice. - That I relied on.

347
00:20:22,980 --> 00:20:26,420
今天赶过来就是要让你别听我的
Well, today I rushed down here to stop you from following it.

348
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:31,300
-你怎么没听我的？ -因为那是个坏主意
- Why didn't you follow it? - Because it was bad advice.

349
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:34,520
好吧，我承认
Okay, I admit it.

350
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:39,460
我当时希望你重新接管我们的家庭
I liked the idea of you coming back and taking over the house, Maggie.

351
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:40,740
我有束缚的感觉
I've been feeling trapped.

352
00:20:41,420 --> 00:20:44,800
你认为心理治疗院是出路？
And you saw Long Island General as a way out?

353
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:47,020
你知道这事了？
You knew about that?

354
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:52,420
我今早出门时碰巧发现这个了
When I was leaving this morning I happened to find this.

355
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:57,840
“接受职位的理由，拒绝职位的理由”
"Reasons to take the job. Reasons to turn it down."

356
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:00,820
-你也看过了吧？ -是的
- Guess you probably read it, too. - Yup.

357
00:21:02,980 --> 00:21:03,920
两边都看了
Both columns.

358
00:21:04,940 --> 00:21:07,460
为什么不告诉我？
Jason, why didn't you tell me about the offer?

359
00:21:08,020 --> 00:21:11,360
我怕你觉得我建议你辞职.
Well, because I didn't want it to seem like I was telling you to quit...

360
00:21:11,360 --> 00:21:14,120
是因为我想把握机会
so that I could pursue my opportunity.

361
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:16,260
我确实是如此
Which I was.

362
00:21:18,060 --> 00:21:20,400
你很想接受哈尔的工作吧？
You really want to take Hal's offer, don't you?

363
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:25,240
我考虑过
I considered it.

364
00:21:25,380 --> 00:21:28,000
于是列了这张表
And then I made out this list and...

365
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:30,540
结果是否定的
it came out clearly against.

366
00:21:31,418 --> 00:21:35,719
杰森，上面有9个理由接受工作 只有1个理由不接受
Jason, it's 9-to-1 in favor of taking the job.

367
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:39,900
是的，但不接受的理由是“因为麦姬”
Yes, but the one reason not to...

368
00:21:40,680 --> 00:21:43,680
这比其他的理由都充分
the one called "Maggie," that's more important to me than all the rest.

369
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:46,440
你真好
You're terrific.

370
00:21:47,868 --> 00:21:49,703
这才是公正的
Hey, well, it's only fair.

371
00:21:49,703 --> 00:21:52,531
轮到我留在家里.
You know, I guess it's my turn to stay home...

372
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:54,720
陪陪<梦幻岛>里面的角色了
with Gilligan, and the Skipper, and the millionaire.

373
00:21:55,442 --> 00:21:56,777
什么？
What?

374
00:21:56,777 --> 00:22:00,240
这个你要问问麦克 他是家里的新哲学家
Well, you gotta ask Mike. He's the new philosopher of the family.

375
00:22:07,740 --> 00:22:11,600
帕罗先生意识到自己普遍地 不受欢迎后.
Mr. Purlow's feelings of paranoia have been greatly reduced...

376
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:16,460
恐惧症大大减轻了
by the realization of the fact that he is indeed universally disliked.

377
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:18,820
-好的方面是.. -爸爸
- On the bright side... - Dad?

378
00:22:19,720 --> 00:22:20,700
我在这里
In here, Carol.

379
00:22:21,301 --> 00:22:23,380
劳动节怎样了？
Hi, honey. How was Career Day?

380
00:22:23,380 --> 00:22:26,800
我发现大部分工作都是悬于一线的
Well, see, I realized that most jobs hang by a slender thread...

381
00:22:27,160 --> 00:22:30,980
于是我决定不采访妈妈 而去采访苏丽凡的爸爸
so I decided not to do Mom's job and I did Emily Sullivan's father's job, instead.

382
00:22:31,140 --> 00:22:34,320
-他做什么的？ -他是劳工部门文员
- What does he do? - He's a clerk at the unemployment office.

383
00:22:35,940 --> 00:22:37,000
爸爸，好消息
Hey, great news, Dad.

384
00:22:37,217 --> 00:22:39,736
我听到过不下百次了
If I heard it once, I heard it a hundred times today.

385
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:43,000
我病了，所有老师都说课堂大不相同
When I was sick, every teacher mentioned that it was not the same there...

386
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:45,720
因为没有我的胡言乱语打扰
without me disrupting class and making stupid comments.

387
00:22:47,780 --> 00:22:50,560
-这算好消息？ -对我来说是
- That's great news? - Yeah, well, it is to me.

388
00:22:50,820 --> 00:22:52,800
也许高一不是因为我而存在
I mean, the 10th grade may not revolve around me...

389
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:54,680
但我不在时，他们绝对知道
but they sure know when I'm not there.

390
00:22:55,420 --> 00:22:57,200
凯罗，<梦幻岛>要开始播放了 这是我们控制以外的事
Hey, Carol, come on. Gilligan's on and we can't stop it.

391
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:03,200
心理学家的一天又结束了
Thus ends another day in the life of a great psychiatrist...

392
00:23:04,140 --> 00:23:08,480
没有置身于大都会的医院中
not behind the facade of a big city hospital, but...

393
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:10,920
而是在此处真实的世界
right here in the real world.

394
00:23:54,058 --> 00:23:57,514
[zeroxia@gmail.com] 2006.04.01
